275s Usage: /usr/bin/kscreen-doctor [options] [output.<name>.<setting> output.<name>.setting [...]]
275s kscreen-doctor allows to change the screen setup from the command-line.
275s 
275s Setting the output configuration is done in an atomic fashion, all settings
275s are applied in a single command.
275s kscreen-doctor can be used to enable and disable outputs, to position screens,
275s change resolution (mode setting), etc.. You should put all your options into 
275s a single invocation of kscreen-doctor, so they can all be applied at once.
275s 
275s Usage examples:
275s 
275s    Show output information:
275s    $ kscreen-doctor -o
275s    Output: 1 eDP-1 enabled connected Panel Modes: Modes: 1:800x600@60 [...] Geometry: 0,0 1280x800
275s    Output: 70 HDMI-2 enabled connected  HDMI Modes: 1:800x600@60 [...] Geometry: 1280,0 1920x1080
275s 
275s    Disable the hdmi output, enable the laptop panel and set it to a specific mode
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.disable output.eDP-1.mode.1 output.eDP-1.enable
275s 
275s    Position the hdmi monitor on the right of the laptop panel
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.position.1280,0 output.eDP-1.position.0,0
275s 
275s    Set resolution mode
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.mode.1920x1080@60 
275s 
275s    Set scale (note: fractional scaling is only supported on wayland)
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.scale.2 
275s 
275s    Set rotation (possible values: none, left, right, inverted, flipped, flipped90, flipped180, flipped270)
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.rotation.left 
275s 
275s    Set HDR mode (possible values: enable, disable)
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.hdr.enable
275s 
275s    Set SDR brightness (possible values: 100-1000)
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.sdr-brightness.300
275s 
275s    Set brightness on non HDR screens (possible values: 0-100)
275s    $ kscreen-doctor output.HDMI-2.brightness.10
